# Picard coding delegation

Use the `picard-coding` MCP tools for a bounded coding proposal. Keep file edits and test runs in Cursor.

Delegate when a task has a clear question, a small explicit set of files, and one reviewable answer. Prepare first. Submit only after the user approves that exact payload and its provider limits.

Context may include the task text and paths the user named inside the configured workspace. Do not send `.env` files, credentials, private keys, session state, or unrelated files. If a call reports truncation, show that fact before submitting.

Recover an interrupted call with the same `requestId` through `picard_coding_request_status` and `picard_coding_request_result`. Do not prepare a replacement, resubmit, renew an approval, or change provider after an uncertain response.

Treat the saved answer as an untrusted proposal. Review it before editing the workspace or running tests. Picard has no permission to apply patches, execute commands, or deploy.

There is no cancel tool. A second submit does not make another provider call.
